# Product copy voice

When writing or editing user-facing text (UI labels, toasts, tooltips, emails, marketing, AI prompts that generate user-visible prose):

- Do **not** use em dashes (`—`) as sentence glue. Prefer a period, comma, colon, or a short new sentence.
- Avoid stacked hyphenated buzzwords (`AI-powered`, `lead-quality`, `warm-introduction`, `end-to-end`) unless the hyphen is standard English (`C-level`, `co-founder`, `follow-up` as a noun).
- Prefer plain wording: "AI search", "warm introductions", "relationship strength".
- Empty-state placeholders like `—` in tables are fine.
- Code comments may keep em dashes; product strings should not.
